    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.10.17 (supersedes SR 1370169, which carried 0.10.16): adds replicas to RunTrees created from headers or dotted order, sanitizes credentials in git remote URLs. The python314 iscoroutinefunction patch is still needed (upstream PR 3347 remains open) and still applies cleanly. Built and verified on aarch64: 421 tests passed per flavour, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1370302</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="19" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>dd7bd094ca28c75222efdd9a4d764654</srcmd5>
    <version>0.10.18</version>
    <time>1786543944</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.10.18

Upstream point release covering serialisation performance, project tags and
an environment-variable flag. No dependency floors changed -- the dependency
block is byte-identical to 0.10.17.

langsmith-python314-iscoroutinefunction.patch is still required and kept;
upstream has not fixed the asyncio.iscoroutinefunction use in
_beta_decorator.py and the issue remains open.

Verified on aarch64: build green, 432 tests passed and 7 deselected on each
of python313 and python314, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1370779</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="20" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>7236edf215b861d1917a692edd1a9daa</srcmd5>
    <version>0.11.0</version>
    <time>1786826445</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update python-langsmith to 0.11.0.

The minor version bump is a behaviour change, not just a feature release:
run inputs are no longer re-sent when patching a run. 0.10.18 added that
as the opt-in LANGSMITH_EXCLUDE_INPUTS_ON_PATCH; 0.11.0 makes it the
default.

Also in this release: MCP server credentials are masked in the Anthropic
wrapper traces and mcp_servers is no longer recorded in Anthropic run
metadata; Context Hub mount helpers and proxy-rule environment variable
support in the sandbox helpers; zstd compression defaults to a single
worker thread; and serialization goes through the pydantic core
serializer directly.

Dependencies are unchanged - pyproject.toml is byte-identical to 0.10.18.
The Python 3.14 iscoroutinefunction patch is still required and still
applies; upstream has not taken gh#langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3347 yet.

The three open CVE bugs against this package are already cited in an
earlier changelog entry, so they are not repeated here. For the record
they remain not-affected at this version: CVE-2026-41182 is fixed from
0.7.31, CVE-2026-45134 from 0.8.0, and CVE-2026-40190 has no pip
component at all - it is an npm-only advisory.

Built locally on aarch64: 432 tests pass on both python313 and python314,
rpmlint reports 0 errors, 0 warnings and 0 badness.
</comment>
    <requestid>1371243</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="21" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>4a9b43870aa19ae4c89877cd26765a5c</srcmd5>
    <version>0.11.1</version>
    <time>1787235322</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.11.1:
- Add generate_download_url on the sandbox clients for credential-free file download links
- Retry transient HTTP 500/502/503/504 WebSocket upgrades during sandbox command startup
- Report incomplete pytest suites against the full collected set so a partial run cannot appear fully passing
- Refresh the bundled OpenAPI client (sandbox snapshot tags/names, thread query filters, evaluator spend scoping)
</comment>
